Data analysis of single and integrated proteomics strategies

MS/MS acquired data are searched against the proper database for peptide identification

using different software indicated in the section 4.2.3 above. Then the results and the spectra are loaded on the software HDExaminer 3.1 where the data is processed, generating the deuterium incorporation of both bound and free protein at different time points and calculating the differential values and heatmaps. The software considers many overlapping peptides cut by pepsin and calculates the minimal region of exchange (a few amino acids) in the sequence, producing a heatmap of the sequence with a differential deuterium incorporation. Such information can also be visualized over the PDB model

